<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Greenfields shares suspended on ASX.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Greenfields shares suspended on ASX.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Stock Exchange said on Monday that share trading in Greenfields Coal Co Ltd had been suspended pending clarification of its financial position.</p>
<p>Greenfields owns a coal extraction plant in West Virginia, United States, and has recently sought funding to help meet the plant's production targets.  </p>
<p>Greenfields is also the subject of a hostile takeover bid by Canada's Mineral Resources Corp.</p>
<p>The company said earlier this month that it had reached a 10-year supply agreement with a unit of Enron Corp, adding to an earlier deal with US Steel.</p>
<p>Greenfields' shares ended at 18.5 cents on Friday, which compared with a 1997 high of 40 cents and a low of 12.5 cents.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
